; Godot resource-scanner ignore marker.
;
; WHY THIS DIRECTORY IS IGNORED
;   addons/godotsteam/ contains a GDExtension that was compiled for an older
;   Godot. Godot 4.4 writes every *.gdextension it finds into
;   .godot/extension_list.cfg and loads them during engine startup, BEFORE any
;   game code runs. Loading that stale DLL crashes the engine:
;
;       CrashHandlerException: Program crashed with signal 11
;       (right after "WorkerThreadPool: N threads")
;
;   Keeping the directory in the repository preserves the original binaries and
;   the load order information, while this marker keeps the engine from ever
;   touching them.
;
; HOW TO ENABLE STEAM NETWORKING (see docs/MULTIPLAYER_PLAN.md)
;   1. Download a Godot 4.4-compatible GodotSteam GDExtension, e.g.
;      https://codeberg.org/godotsteam/godotsteam/releases/tag/v4.17.1-gde
;   2. Replace the binaries in win64/ (and add linux/ or osx/ if you ship them).
;   3. Delete this .gdignore file.
;   4. Re-open the project in the editor once so Godot rebuilds
;      .godot/extension_list.cfg, then confirm Engine.has_singleton("Steam").
;
;   No game code needs to change: NetworkManager already detects the singleton
;   at runtime and TransportFactory falls back to ENet when it is missing.
